course: dictionary
lesson: 6653
title: Numerous: many, but not counted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Numerous means very many, a great number of things or people. «Lanternfish have light organs called photophores along their bodies, and they are among the most common fish on Earth; only the tiny bristlemouths may be more numerous.» Here numerous tells you there are a lot of fish, but it does not say how many.
explain: Writers use numerous in formal writing, reports and exams, where lots of or many might sound too casual. You can say numerous mistakes, numerous times or on numerous occasions. Try swapping in many: if the sentence still works, numerous is the more formal choice.
explain: Be careful: numerous does not give a number. If a maths problem says «Sam has numerous marbles», you cannot add or count with it, because numerous is not an exact amount. When you need to calculate, look for real numbers like twelve or forty.
explain: Numerous has a second, formal meaning: made up of many people or things. «The Mole makes each of them recite the names of his numerous brothers» tells us the Mole has a big family. The clue is brothers, which shows many people.
fact: Numerous means very many, or a great number of.
fact: «Numerous» does not give an exact number, so it cannot be used for calculating.
fact: Numerous can also mean made up of many people or things, as in «his numerous brothers».
fact: «Numerous» is common in formal writing, reports and exams, instead of «lots of» or «many».
fact: Phrases to know: on numerous occasions, numerous times, too numerous to count.
exercise: «Sam has numerous marbles.» How many marbles does Sam have? | Exactly twelve | Exactly forty | *We cannot tell an exact number, only that there are many
exercise: Which phrase means happening many times? | on one occasion only | in a single minute | before lunch | *on numerous occasions
exercise: Ella says numerous is just a fancy word for lots of. Is she right? | *Mostly right, but numerous is more formal and does not give an exact number | Wrong, numerous means heavy | Wrong, numerous means quiet | Wrong, numerous means exactly ten
test: The school report said there were «numerous complaints» about litter. What does numerous tell us? | Exactly one complaint | *Many complaints, but not exactly how many | Exactly two complaints | No complaints at all
test: «Her numerous cousins came to the party.» What does numerous suggest here? | Only two cousins | A cousin who was late | *A great many cousins, or a large family | Cousins who were sad
exam: Which is the best reason to choose numerous over many in a formal report? | It is only used in stories for children | It gives an exact count of the things | It is shorter and means fewer | *It sounds more formal, and it shows many without giving a number
